@startuml
title MODRISS End-to-End Process — Development/Delivery + Operations/Maintenance
skinparam backgroundColor #F5F3ED
start
|Development and Delivery|
:e2e.ph0 — Phase 0: Inception, Tailoring & Organization;
fork
  :e2e.ph1 — Phase 1: Active Product Construction & Evolution;
  repeat
    :e2e.p0..p7 — Model-driven increment activities;
    :e2e.rel.a1..a3 — Release and transition activities;
    :G7 sends accepted release to Operations and Maintenance;
  repeat while (Next release selected and retirement not authorized?) is (next release)
  :e2e.ph2 — Phase 2: Retire, Migrate & Close;
fork again
  |Operations and Maintenance|
  repeat
    :e2e.ops.a1 — Operate and Observe;
    :e2e.ops.a2 — Kanban Service-Delivery;
    :e2e.ops.a3 — Incident, Problem and Risk Response;
    :e2e.ops.a4 — Maintenance Change and Reconciliation;
    :e2e.ops.a5 — Service and Process Improvement;
    note right: The accepted baseline remains in operation\nwhile later releases are developed.
  repeat while (Any live release remains?) is (yes)
end fork
|Development and Delivery|
:G8 closes both processes;
stop
@enduml
